From: AutoBleem <autobleem@retromenele.pl>
Subject: [PATCH] input_keymaps: the PlayStation Classic's POWER button (KEY_SLEEP) as the "power" key

The console's front buttons are keyboard keys: POWER is KEY_SLEEP (SDL: SDL_SCANCODE_SLEEP), RESET is
KEY_PLAYPAUSE ("play" in RetroArch's key names), OPEN is KEY_EJECTCD. RetroArch maps only KEY_POWER to
RETROK_POWER, so RetroBoot's `input_exit_emulator = "power"` never matched the button on a stock build.
KEY_SLEEP (udev) and SDLK_SLEEP (the sdl2 input driver) are RETROK_POWER too now; with
`input_exit_emulator = "power"` POWER quits RetroArch - the launcher takes over - and with
`input_menu_toggle = "play"` RESET opens the menu over the game.
---
diff --git a/input/input_keymaps.c b/input/input_keymaps.c
index 972acc2..dc892c8 100644
--- a/input/input_keymaps.c
+++ b/input/input_keymaps.c
@@ -792,6 +792,10 @@ const struct rarch_key_map rarch_key_map_sdl[] = {
    { SDLK_PAUSE, RETROK_BREAK },
    { SDLK_MENU, RETROK_MENU },
    { SDLK_POWER, RETROK_POWER },
+#ifdef HAVE_SDL2 /* SDLK_SLEEP is an enumerator, not a macro */
+   /* the PlayStation Classic's POWER button (KEY_SLEEP) through SDL */
+   { SDLK_SLEEP, RETROK_POWER },
+#endif
 
 #ifndef HAVE_SDL2
    { SDLK_EURO, RETROK_EURO },
@@ -1358,6 +1362,8 @@ const struct rarch_key_map rarch_key_map_linux[] = {
    { KEY_BREAK, RETROK_BREAK },
    { KEY_MENU, RETROK_MENU },
    { KEY_POWER, RETROK_POWER },
+   /* the PlayStation Classic's POWER button is KEY_SLEEP: the same "power" key name */
+   { KEY_SLEEP, RETROK_POWER },
 #ifndef ANDROID
    { KEY_EURO, RETROK_EURO },
 #endif
